1269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (I love to sketch wireframes by hand before digitizing them. This process can be automated by taking a photo of a sketch and having AI convert the sketch into a digitized wireframe. There are also text to wireframe tools. Predictive wireframing where as you actively create your wireframe, other elements are immediately added based on what common patterns are- just like predictive text on your phone or document editor.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The most successful tools will integrate into designers' existing workflows. This likely means they are built on top of Figma or have an export to Figma feature.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Impact)
/E (Impact)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Today, AI's impact results in hours to many days saved. In the future, wireframe time could be reduced by 90% as more data is gathered about how wireframes are built and integrated into the models. Wireframing is likely to become an almost automatic and effortless part of any process in the future with minimal work required.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2605 0 R
/ActualText (This is advantageous because it will also allow designers to dedicate more time to the creative aspects of their jobs. They can also explore more inventive approaches to problem-solving since the fundamental elements will be handled for them.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
