1285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Writing documentation is the bane of many product managers. I hate it. LLMs are particularly good at text. Most requirements documents are used for basic internal alignment, but collect dust shortly after creation. This makes documentation a fantastic use case for offloading to AI tools.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Impact)
/E (Impact)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (90-95% of the time it takes to build out requirements documents can be saved via AI tools. Most of the effort in Product Requirement Documents \(PRDs\) and other documentation is spent on formatting filler and existing requirements. Many enterprise software applications have reusable components from across the enterprise, such as sign-on requirements.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
