1980 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Sharing knowledge and best practices across your organization is essential to unlock the full potential of AI in product development. Here are three ideas:)
/Pg 113 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1981 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2821 0 R
/ActualText (Communities of Practice: Establish internal communities where team members with a common interest in AI share their experiences, exchange ideas and collaborate on solving problems. Slack channels, consistent meetings and workshops can be used to facilitate.)
/Pg 113 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1982 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2822 0 R
/ActualText (Documentation and Lessons Learned: Encourage teams to document their experiences, challenges, and successful implementations. Making this information accessible to other teams through knowledge repositories on Sharepoint, Notion or just announcing in Slack will allow for broader visibility and learning.)
/Pg 113 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1983 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2823 0 R
/ActualText (Learning Opportunities: Provide opportunities for continuous learning and growth through training sessions, workshops, and conferences. Support team members' participation in external events related to AI enables them to stay up-to-date with the latest trends and technologies.)
/Pg 113 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1984 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (You must enable teams to experiment, share knowledge, and collaborate effectively. Foster a culture of experimentation. Piar senior and junior team members. Promote knowledge sharing. Before you know it, your teams will be flying with their thousand AI interns.)
/E (You must enable teams to experiment, share knowledge, and collaborate effectively. Foster a culture of experimentation. Piar senior and junior team members. Promote knowledge sharing. Before you know it, your teams will be flying with their thousand AI interns.)
